From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:45:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 130/138] media: apple: t7000 ISP: wedge hunt knobs after
 CH_START

H2/H2b wedge the whole SoC within ~50 ms of a successful CH_START (last
traced write = the routine mailbox ack 0xc050c, written 22x before in the
same run). Static RE of the DART kext points at the dart-isp SMMU block:
iOS setTranslationEnable (0x7fe35a8 -> 0x7fe361c) sets SMMU+0xc
byte[sid] |= 0x80 right after the DART TCR and never writes SMMU TTBRs;
we leave it 0, so the pipeline DMA is likely not translated.

- SMMU fault check on every DART fault check (SMMU+0x10 bit 31, logged
  with +0x14/+0x18/+0x1c, acked with status & 0x0c00006c like iOS);
  not fatal for the IO channel. Default on (reads only, plus the ack).
- smmu_en=1: save the old SMMU+0xc, verify the enable bits stuck, and
  restore it before the DART tables are torn down.
- DART log: fix the diag(+0x20)/fetch(+0x30) labels (they were
  swapped), add DART/SMMU bypass (+0x2c) and the SMMU error status.
- trace=1: print buffered fw TERMINAL lines after every command (they
  were printed only after the START ioctl, so a wedge lost all of them).
- dart_ios=1: DART diag 0x100, fetch 0xe0303, bypass 0, SMMU bypass 0,
  as the iOS DART restore does (restored at fini).
- quiet_ms=N: after CH_START no ISP register access for N ms (IRQ
  masked, no mailbox ack, no doorbell), DRAM-only TERMINAL drain and a
  heartbeat line every 10 ms: splits an async wedge from an AP access.
- stream_nobufs=1: CH_START without posting frame/meta buffers.
- canary=1: before CH_START, log which RAM pages sit at canary_base +
  the frame/RAW IOVAs (where a bypassed DMA would land) and watch their
  hashes during quiet_ms. Reads only, NOMAP memory skipped.

All new knobs default off. Not tested on hardware.

